# Worker bindings for `pnpm preview` and the local acceptance harnesses.
#
# Copy this to `.dev.vars` at the repository root, where the integration suite
# reads `.env`. The names and their meanings are the same, so see `.env.example`
# for what each one is; this file exists only because Wrangler will not read
# that one.
#
# Wrangler does not read the root copy directly, which surprised several rounds
# of this project: it resolves `.dev.vars` against the directory of its config
# file, and `pnpm preview` runs `--config .output/server/wrangler.json`. So
# `pnpm preview` stages this file into `.output/server/` first
# (`scripts/stage-preview-secrets.mjs`); before it did, a correctly copied root
# `.dev.vars` reached the previewed Worker through nothing at all, and every
# authored request answered 503 (#274).
#
# So edit the root copy, never the staged one. Anything added only under
# `.output/server/` is transient — the next build rebuilds that directory and
# the next preview restages over it, and it will work right up until it
# silently does not. The root copy is the source of truth; the staging step
# says so out loud when it replaces a staged file that differs.
#
# `nuxt dev` reads `.env`, and additionally adopts the NUXT_-prefixed names
# here into its own environment (`build/devVarsModule.ts`) — otherwise they
# would reach the proxied Cloudflare bindings and never reach runtimeConfig,
# and screen creation would answer 503 under plain `pnpm dev` while every test
# stayed green. A name already set in `.env` or the shell wins.
#
# One of them is load-bearing for a local acceptance run:
# NUXT_SCREEN_OUTPUT_CAPABILITY_SIGNING_KEY. Without it, capability minting and
# Screen Output delivery answer 503, and `pnpm test:delivery:graphics` never
# reaches anything to assert.
#
# NUXT_ABLY_API_KEY is the one name here that reaches a third party, so leave it
# empty unless you have a real key. Neither wrong state announces itself in the
# response: empty, a Screen command answers a bare 500, because that route has
# nothing to do but publish and `mapPublicNitroError` sanitises the cause out of
# any 500; filled with a placeholder, only the empty string reads as absent, so
# the key passes for configured and Ably refuses each publish with 404 code
# 40400. That silence is why the name is written here rather than left to be
# discovered from a failure.

NUXT_SCREEN_OUTPUT_CAPABILITY_SIGNING_KEY=""
NUXT_GRAPHICS_ADMIN_TOKEN=""
NUXT_ABLY_API_KEY=""
